From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Eggleston <eggnet@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:16:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] server: Keep the request's status when receive_fd() drops a
 stale fd.

thread_get_inflight_fd() calls receive_fd() until the fd it looks for
has arrived, and receive_fd() can first read an fd that a thread sent
just before it was killed. get_thread_from_id() fails for that thread
and sets STATUS_INVALID_CID, which then becomes the status of the
request being handled. A new_thread request creates the thread and its
handle but returns STATUS_INVALID_CID, so NtCreateThreadEx() fails and
the handle leaks.

Restore the request's status after the lookup. The stale fd is dropped
as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 server/request.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/request.c b/server/request.c
index b42a16fff14..8c433c6eca8 100644
--- a/server/request.c
+++ b/server/request.c
@@ -409,7 +409,13 @@ int receive_fd( struct process *process )
     {
         struct thread *thread;
 
-        if (data.tid) thread = get_thread_from_id( data.tid );
+        if (data.tid)
+        {
+            /* the sender may be gone already, which must not fail the current request */
+            unsigned int error = get_error();
+            thread = get_thread_from_id( data.tid );
+            set_error( error );
+        }
         else thread = (struct thread *)grab_object( get_process_first_thread( process ));
 
         if (!thread || thread->process != process || thread->state == TERMINATED)
